 QT2S: Qatar Traffic Social Sensing
 ----------------------------------
 This project is about the identification of Qatar traffic related tweets.
 The overall objective is to listen to Twitter live steam for all traffic-related tweets in Qatar, then
 enrich those tweets with new metadata such as: location names, geo-coordinates, etc.

 There are three main classes so far (will add new one in the future):

  1. TwitterCollector: collects tweets from Twitter stream.
  2. TwitterClassifier: classifies a tweet into traffic/non-traffic related.
  3. TwitterLocationER: extracts named location entities from the tweet body.


 Dependencies
 ------------
 1. Redis (for queueing and messaging.)
 2. NLTK (for text processing: tokenization, etc.)
 3. Tweepy (Twitter streaming API for tweets collection.)

 How to run
 ----------
 1. Start Redis server.
 2. Make sure NLTK has all required data (some  tokenizers may need specific packages).
 3. Run QT2S.py to start (this will trigger three separate processes)
 	TwitterCollector ---> Queue1 >--- TwitterClassifier ---> Queue2 >----- TwitterLocationER ----> Queue3

 REDIS QUEUES
 -------------
 Use default connection parameters: host='localhost', port=6379, db=0
 Namespace: QMIC
 Names:
	Queue1: raw_tweets
	Queue2: traffic_tweets
	Queue3: geocoded_tweets


 	********


